xnu 0193: expand draw-state groups inside the nested indirect buffers too

0186 rewrote CP_SET_DRAW_STATE only in the stream Mesa hands to the user client,
but the group that wedges the CP lives in the nested indirect buffer that stream
chains (0x10434000, a 27-group CP_SET_DRAW_STATE). The rings say it plainly: a
71-dword stream completes in 13 ms, and the 168-dword one whose nested IB
carries that group never answers its fence; 0191 then marks the GPU stopped so
the system survives (measured: the UI kept drawing at 26 fps with the CPU).

Expand both levels: every nested CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER target is expanded into a
scratch arena and the packet is patched to point at it with its new dword count,
then the top-level stream is expanded the same way and submitted from the arena.
A group is a list of register/value pairs in GPU memory and the CP executes
those as type-4 register writes, which is what the rest of the stream uses.

